WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.326
Three examples show why names are clues rather than contracts.

2
00:00:04.326 --> 00:00:09.489
C V sixty four A six zero is the example on the current nomenclature page.

3
00:00:09.489 --> 00:00:20.723
C V thirty two A six zero X is a real configuration name, but the current introduction calls that part number interim while the team decides the issue direction.

4
00:00:20.723 --> 00:00:32.166
C V thirty two E four zero P is historically easy to decompose, yet its implemented behavior and released parameter sets must come from the current CV32E40P manual.

5
00:00:32.166 --> 00:00:35.725
A readable name is not a frozen product definition.

